  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">The Internet Protocol version 4 (IPv4) <xref target="RFC791" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC791"/> provides for
expansion of the protocol by supporting a number of &quot;options&quot; in the
variable-length IPv4 header.  IPv4 options are identified by an
option &quot;type&quot; value, whose registration is managed by IANA <xref target="IANA-IP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IANA-IP"/>.
A number of IPv4 options have become obsolete in practice, but have
never been formally deprecated.  This document deprecates such IPv4
options, thus cleaning up the corresponding IANA registry.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">This document also obsoletes <xref target="RFC1385" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1385"/>, <xref target="RFC1393" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1393"/>, <xref target="RFC1475" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1475"/>, and
<xref target="RFC1770" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1770"/>, and requests that the RFC Editor change their status to
Historic.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="discussion-of-deprecated-options" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-discussion-of-deprecated-options">Discussion of Deprecated Options</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">The following subsections discuss the options being deprecated.  No
other reference information has been found.</t>
      <section anchor="stream-id" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.1">
        <name slugifiedName="name-stream-id">Stream ID</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.1-1">The Stream ID option is obsolete.  It is specified in RFC 791
<xref target="RFC791" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC791"/>, and is deprecated in Section 3.2.1.8 of RFC 1122 <xref target="RFC1122" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1122"/>
and Section 4.2.2.1 of RFC 1812 <xref target="RFC1812" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1812"/>.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="extended-internet-protocol" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.2">
        <name slugifiedName="name-extended-internet-protocol">Extended Internet Protocol</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.2-1">The Extended Internet Protocol option is defined in <xref target="RFC1385" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1385"/> and is
superseded by <xref target="RFC2460" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2460"/>.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="traceroute" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.3">
        <name slugifiedName="name-traceroute">Traceroute</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.3-1">The Traceroute option is defined in <xref target="RFC1393" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1393"/>.  The Traceroute option
is defined as Experimental; it was never widely deployed on the
public Internet.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="encode" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.4">
        <name slugifiedName="name-encode">ENCODE</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.4-1">This option was used for experimentation around IP-layer encryption.
No products are known to ever have shipped with support for this
option.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="visa" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.5">
        <name slugifiedName="name-visa">VISA</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.5-1">This option was part of an experiment <xref target="VISA87" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="VISA87"/> <xref target="VISA89" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="VISA89"/> at USC and
was never widely deployed.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="address-extension" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.6">
        <name slugifiedName="name-address-extension">Address Extension</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.6-1">The Address Extension option is defined in an Experimental RFC
<xref target="RFC1475" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1475"/> and marked as IPv7.  IPv7 was never widely deployed.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="selective-directed-broadcast" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.7">
        <name slugifiedName="name-selective-directed-broadcast">Selective Directed Broadcast</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.7-1">The Selective Directed Broadcast option was originally defined in
<xref target="RFC1770" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1770"/>.  This option was never widely deployed and the approach
was abandoned.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="dynamic-packet-state" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.8">
        <name slugifiedName="name-dynamic-packet-state">Dynamic Packet State</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.8-1">The Dynamic Packet State option was specified in <xref target="DIFFSERV-DPS" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="DIFFSERV-DPS"/>.  The
aforementioned document was meant to be published as Experimental,
but it never became an RFC.  The IP option was never widely deployed.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="upstream-multicast-pkt." numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.9">
        <name slugifiedName="name-upstream-multicast-pkt.">Upstream Multicast Pkt.</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.9-1">This option was originally specified in <xref target="BIDIR-PIM" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="BIDIR-PIM"/>.  Its use was
deprecated by <xref target="RFC5015" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5015"/>, which employs a control-plane mechanism to
solve the problem of doing upstream forwarding of multicast packets
on a multi-access LAN.</t>
      </section>
    </section>
    <section anchor="iana-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3">
      <name slugifiedName="name-iana-considerations">IANA Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-1">The &quot;IP OPTION NUMBERS&quot; registry <xref target="IANA-IP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IANA-IP"/> contains the list of
currently assigned IP option numbers.  This registry also denotes a
deprecated IP Option Number by marking it with a footnote.</t>
