      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-4">The IP options &quot;MTU Probe&quot; (MTUP, value 11) and &quot;MTU Reply&quot; (MTUR,
value 12) were initially defined in <xref target="RFC1063" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1063"/> and have already been
deprecated by <xref target="RFC1191" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1191"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="changing-the-status-of-the-corresponding-rfcs-to-historic" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4">
      <name slugifiedName="name-changing-the-status-of-the-corresponding-rfcs-to-historic">Changing the Status of the Corresponding RFCs to Historic</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-1">Per this document, the RFC Editor has changed the status of
<xref target="RFC1385" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1385"/>, <xref target="RFC1393" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1393"/>, <xref target="RFC1475" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1475"/>, and <xref target="RFC1770" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1770"/> to Historic.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="security-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-5">
      <name slugifiedName="name-security-considerations">Security Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-1">This document does not modify the security properties of the IPv4
options being deprecated.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="acknowledgments" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-6">
